<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan money market rates stay high.</title>
<headline>Pakistan money market rates stay high.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's interbank money market rates remained high on Thursday owing to a paucity of funds, dealers said.</p>
<p>The overnight rates remained at 20 percent despite the maturity of securities worth 11 billion rupees, one dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;The short-term borrowing rates denote the impending dryer spell in the days to come,&quot; the dealer said.</p>
<p>Banks were seen at the central bank's discount window at the close of trading hours, the dealer said.</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
